WEBVTT

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:41.800
In ancient times, when the ancestor of the Queen descended from Ephon Noha to Tahai Aze,

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.910
the kingdoms of the land were on the verge of perishing,

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:51.140
due to the war which caused a low populace and infertile land.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:58.690
When the Founding King walked through the field littered with corpses,

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:05.730
above him, a beast-lord that usually would not be tame to humans, flew as if it were protecting him.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:15.380
Also in the water were Touda with sharp, venomous fangs, that bowed their heads to him, and gave him way.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:31.230
Erin came to the summer cabin with Jone, and was fascinated by a creature called a beast-lord that a guest, Kalon, had described.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:42.870
When Erin saw a beast-lord flying high above her head, her fascination with them increased.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.130
A beast-lord?

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.680
It smells great.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.310
It's ready now.

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:55.520
Ittadakimasu!

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:59.260
It's hot!

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.050
Itadakimasu!

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:06.720
It's hot!

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.150
Iz hoth, buth iz good!

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:14.210
There's plenty more.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:21.920
Erin, I'll be out gathering some chigo tomorrow.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.600
"Chigo?"

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:25.690
Yeah.  It's a medicinal herb.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:31.420
The chigo's root works wonders on inflammations of organs.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:36.150
Are you not well, Oji-san?

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:40.630
No, no.  I'm gathering some in order to sell them.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:45.020
A single chigo root can get us one large gold nugget.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.570
"One large gold nugget?!"

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.100
That's amazing!

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.140
We'll go with you, old man.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.360
It's said that chigo lives on Touda breath.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.820
"Touda breath?"

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:06.180
It's a medicinal herb that grows in deep valleys where Touda live.

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:15.010
No thanks.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:17.380
We changed our minds!  We won't go!

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.940
Oji-san, are there Touda where you're going?

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.530
I'll come too!

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.190
Don't worry.

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:38.130
I'll climb down into the valley using a rope, but I won't go all the way down to where the Touda are.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:40.870
But...

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:45.680
What's with the look?  Touda will run away after a fart of mine.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:06.930
The Valley of the Beast-Lord

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:20.790
When I found her,

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:26.070
I caught the scent of Touda coming from the mud covering her.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.480
That expression of hers...

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:37.710
What happened with her and Touda?

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.210
Oji-san!

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:11.140
Oji-san...

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.400
"<i>I'll be back by evening.</i>

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:23.980
<i>Jone.</i>"

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.320
Nukku-san!

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:56.600
Do you know where chigo blooms?

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.340
Chigo?

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:01.900
No, I don't.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:06.040
But we <i>do</i> know a valley where Touda live.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.500
Where is that?!

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.290
Little girl!

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:21.370
Hey!  Wait for us!

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.500
Little girl!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.310
There's a chigo.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:07.880
Looks like there aren't any Touda around here, but it's better to be safe than sorry.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:19.510
Now that's definitely a hekusokazura berry.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.720
It makes my farts smell sweet.

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:28.940
No wonder animals don't come near this.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:32.190
<i>"I'll be back by evening."</i>

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:01.470
Oji-san!

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:05.490
Oji-san!!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:17.690
Oji-san!

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:19.150
Oji-san!

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:20.610
Oji-san!

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.110
Oji-san!!

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.240
Oji-san, are you all right?!

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:41.400
Erin...

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:45.900
Your leg?

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:47.680
Your leg hurts?

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:52.900
Yeah.  And it looks like I hit my back and waist pretty hard.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:08.510
Oji-san!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:11.040
I thought you were dead.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:17.450
Sorry.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:21.320
I made you worry.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:36.130
Where am I?

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.660
Halfway down the cliff.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:41.140
You're on a ledge.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.130
W-What's this?

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:50.400
I brought your blanket.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:55.020
Mountain weather is quick to change, so I thought it might be needed.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:59.250
Thank you, Erin.

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:10.970
Erin, go back up the cliff before it gets dark.

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:15.150
You don't have to worry about me.

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:18.710
No!  I'll stay here with you!

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.860
You...  idiot.

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:27.530
If you remain, you'll never know when you might fall off this small ledge.

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.660
I'll be fine!

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:52.390
Hey, a shooting star!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.140
Aren't you cold?

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:56.250
I'm fine.

00:14:57.090 --> 00:14:59.980
It's my first time going to bed while gazing at the stars.

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:04.460
It feels like they're watching over us.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:08.550
Sleeping outside is not bad, Oji-san.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.130
Yeah.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.250
<i>It's so warm. </i>

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:24.940
<i>Mom. </i>

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.590
<i>What do I smell like? </i>

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:30.490
<i>Let's see...</i>

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.180
<i>Smells like the sun.</i>

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:38.420
Do I smell like the sun?

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.310
"The sun?"

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:42.880
Yeah, you do.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.360
You smell like the gentle sun.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:33.110
Touda!

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:41.560
They're after the baby!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:16:59.660
Oh no!

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:02.140
The baby's going to be eaten!

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:14.030
Stop!

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:15.640
Don't eat the baby!

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:16.510
Erin?

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.620
Please, stop!

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:56.530
<i>Mom!!</i>

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:29.430
Erin!

00:19:25.030 --> 00:19:26.560
It's a beast-lord.

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:31.830
That's a beast-lord?

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:38.770
I never thought I'd get the chance to see a wild beast-lord.

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:03.120
That's...

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.740
a beast-lord...

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:14.010
With the figure of the beast-lord so close up,

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:20.260
Erin couldn't help but see in it her mother, Soyon.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:26.300
Ani!  They're here!  I found them!

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:29.270
We'll help you up now!

00:20:33.970 --> 00:20:37.140
Man, it's great that you're okay.

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:39.260
We were very worried about you.

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.220
That noise...

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:50.690
The Touda stopped moving when they heard that noise.

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:10.140
That other time, too.

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:15.270
<i>Hang on tight, Erin. </i>

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:19.230
<i>You must never do what I'm about to do. </i>

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:25.530
<i>Since I'm about to commit an unforgivable crime.</i>

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:30.120
That sound.

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:33.380
That cry.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:42.590
Mom must have controlled the Touda with her finger whistle.

00:21:46.060 --> 00:21:47.860
Erin, let's go.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:13.800
When Erin saw the beast-lord control the Touda in order to save her child,

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:19.920
she wondered why Soyon hesitated to blow her finger whistle.

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:27.310
But it was not until much later that she found the answer.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:02.950
My name is Nason.

00:24:04.220 --> 00:24:09.160
I'm an Explorer for the Mist People who drifts with the mist and lives abiding by our code.

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:16.380
I've been away from the Mist People for many years
following Erin, the daughter of my former fiancée, Soyon,

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:20.540
to observe what she sees and feels.

00:24:21.780 --> 00:24:25.050
Kemono no Souja Erin.  Mist People.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:30.030
Mist People
